This is a giant Battleship board game, a game played on a board. HTSUS 9504.90 covers other articles for arcade, table or parlor games. Within 9504.90, the subheading 9504.90.40 covers "Tables for casino games and automatic bowling alley equipment; parts and accessories thereof", and 9504.90.60 covers "Other" (including board games). Subheading 9504.90.20 is for "Video game consoles", which does not apply. The statistical suffix 9504.90.6000 is the standard one for board games such as Battleship.

Classification of the 5-foot version is not a given, though. It could be argued to be a lawn game or a game of skill played at a larger scale, but it is still a parlor or table-type game, and CBP generally classifies these in 9504.90.60.

{"hts_code": "9504.90.6000", "reason": "The oversized Battleship game is a board game of the parlor/table type, which falls under heading 9504 as other games, in subheading 9504.90.60."}
